<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jahangir Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1628">1628</a>–<a href="/years/1652">1652</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Salqam Jahangir</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jahangir">Jahangir</a> Khan was khan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazakhs">Kazakhs</a> from 1628 to 1652 and a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esim-khan">Esim Khan</a>. In 1643, with a small force armed with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/musket">muskets</a> and help from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yalangtush-bahadur">Yalangtush Bahadur</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a>, he is said to have checked the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzungars">Dzungar</a> ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erdeni-batur">Erdeni Batur</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-orbulaq">Battle of Orbulaq</a> in the mountains of Zhetysu. He was killed fighting the Dzungars in 1652.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jahangir-khan.jpg" alt="Jahangir Khan" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TheAsianAwards · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jahangir_Khan_2018.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
